course: dictionary
lesson: 3208
title: Enjoy: liking and having fun
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Enjoy means to like doing something, or to get pleasure from it. When you enjoy a game, you are having fun with it. «Enjoy yourself» means have a good time, and people say «Enjoy your meal!» as a kind wish.
explain: Enjoy can also mean to have something good. «The town enjoys sunny weather» means the town has plenty of sunshine. It does not mean the town likes the weather. Ask yourself: is someone liking something, or does something good just belong to them?
explain: Look at the words around enjoy to find its meaning. «He enjoyed the game more» is about liking. Enjoy changes its form too: enjoys, enjoyed, enjoying, enjoyable, enjoyment.
fact: Enjoy is a verb: I enjoy, he enjoys, we enjoyed, they are enjoying.
fact: «Enjoyable» is an adjective, and it describes something that is fun to do.
fact: «Enjoyment» is a noun, and it means the feeling of having pleasure.
fact: «Enjoy yourself» means have a good time.
exercise: «Languages keep changing, borrowing and playing, so the best language skill is curiosity: notice odd words, ask what they mean and enjoy how people talk.» What does enjoy mean here? | To stop how people talk | To pay money for how people talk | *To like listening to how people talk | To forget how people talk
exercise: «Clubs are for fun and learning, so the best choice depends on what the child enjoys, not on what other families do.» Which meaning of enjoy fits here? | Is good at sums | Has a lot of money | *Likes or takes pleasure in | Is very tired of
exercise: Mum says, «Enjoy your meal!» What does she mean? | Eat it all up quickly | Do not spill your food | Your meal is too cold | *I hope you have a good time eating
test: In «he enjoyed the game more», what does enjoyed mean? | Was tired of the game | Lost the game | *Had pleasure from the game | Watched the game from far away
test: «The town enjoys sunny weather.» Which meaning of enjoy is this? | To be sad about something | To like doing something | *To have something good | To have a good time
exam: Grandad says, «So read the Wild Wood like a naturalist: enjoy the story, then ask what the real animal would be doing.» What does enjoy mean? | *To like and take pleasure in | To skip it quickly | To read it aloud | To make a copy of it
